<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Release-scoped upgrade data for Darpan 1.5.0.
Assembled from the generic seed files under runtime/component/darpan/data/ over the range
v1.4.0..v1.5.0, then hand-ordered. Load with: ./gradlew loadDarpanUpgradeData

ORDERING: hand-verified parent-before-child, and it matters in three places. Moqui's entity-facade
loader inserts rows in DOCUMENT ORDER — it does not topologically sort — so a child ahead of its
parent fails with a raw *_ibfk_* constraint error that points nowhere near this file. The three
chains are: EnumerationType before its Enumerations; a parent Enumeration before any Enumeration
naming it in parentEnumId (a self-reference); and Enumeration before SourceSystemConnector before
SourceSystemConnectorField. release_preflight.py sorts alphabetically and WILL break all three if
this file is regenerated. Re-order by hand afterwards.

OPERATOR IMPACT: 54 records. Additive except for three deliberate restatements of rows that already
exist in every deployed environment (create-or-update by primary key, so they change only the named
column):

  - Enumeration OMS and SHOPIFY are restated with their readable descriptions, "HotWax" and
    "Shopify". Deployed databases hold the shouty "SHOPIFY", which is what an operator sees wherever
    a system is named — "Extracting SHOPIFY", "Missing from SHOPIFY", and the compared-files labels.
    The seed file has been correct for some time; only the stored rows are stale. These fix FUTURE
    runs only: a run's file labels are stamped into its output document when it executes, so
    historical runs keep the name they were stamped with (decision, 2026-08-13).
  - Enumeration OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS, which shipped in 1.4.0, gains parentEnumId="OMS" so it groups
    under HotWax in the two-step source picker. Until this loads, transfer orders appear as a
    top-level system rather than as an endpoint of HotWax.

Everything else is new capability. Until this file loads on an upgraded environment:

  - No config can be shared across tenants. A grant must name a configTypeEnumId that exists, so
    every attempt fails on config_tenant_access_ibfk_2 — and it fails for all four config types,
    not just the one that was tried.
  - A tenant admin cannot save a Slack chat space; save#TenantChatSpace checks the provider catalog
    first and reports "The chat provider catalog is not loaded on this deployment". Google Chat
    spaces are unaffected either way: chatProviderEnumId is nullable and a null provider resolves to
    CHAT_PROV_GOOGLE, so every space that exists today keeps delivering with or without this file.
  - Databases, the OMS reconciliationOrders and reconciliationReturns endpoints, and the Shopify
    return-reference extractor do not appear as selectable sources, and their extract services are
    not dispatchable — the security allow-list is derived from enabled connector rows.
  - The rules board offers no field pills for any endpoint, because the pill list moved out of
    Groovy constants into SourceSystemConnectorField rows.
  - The Migrations screen lists nothing and run#PendingMigrations does nothing, because the registry
    it walks is empty.

NO BACKFILL, AND NO CREDENTIALS — DELIBERATE. Two things that could have been data are services
instead, because their values are per-tenant secrets or per-tenant ids that must not be baked into a
release artifact:

  - Cross-tenant sharing is granted through the product ("Shared with" on the config edit form,
    facade.ConfigSharingFacadeServices.grant#ConfigTenantAccess), which enforces a two-sided gate —
    the acting user must hold DARPAN_TENANT_ADMIN in BOTH tenants. Pre-seeding a grant would mean
    committing production tenant and config ids to this file, and a row naming the wrong tenant
    would silently widen access. Both tenants must also live in the SAME deployment:
    ConfigTenantAccess is a row referencing tenants in its own database.
  - Copying each chat space's legacy googleChatWebhookUrl into the provider-agnostic webhookUrl
    column is done by migrate#ChatSpaceWebhookUrls, now registered in the migration registry below.
    It is OPTIONAL for this release — resolveWebhookUrl falls back to the legacy column.

Consequently this file is safe to load unconditionally and needs no verification step.

ONE-TIME SERVICES: this release replaces "run these by hand" with a registry. After loading, run
admin migration run#PendingMigrations once (or use the Migrations screen); it is idempotent, walks
the six registered migrations in sequence, skips any already applied, and records each in a ledger
written in a forced-new transaction so a failure survives rollback. That covers 1.2.0's
migrate#TenantNotificationSettings and 1.3.0's migrate#AutomationExcludeFilters, so an environment
behind on those no longer needs to chase them individually.

PREREQUISITE: 1.4.0 upgrade-data must be loaded first. This file is release-scoped and does not
re-carry 1.4.0's three records (AUT_WIN_STATE, the OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS enum, and its connector row)
— it only amends the transfer-order enum, which a create-or-update will happily insert in full if
the row is absent, but the connector row it needs would still be missing.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">

    <!-- Enumeration types first: every Enumeration below FKs its type. -->
    <moqui.basic.EnumerationType enumTypeId="DarpanChatProvider"
            description="Chat products Darpan can post run notifications to"/>
    <moqui.basic.EnumerationType enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"
            description="Darpan API source config types that support cross-tenant sharing"/>

    <!-- Chat destination providers. TenantChatSpace.chatProviderEnumId FKs these. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="CHAT_PROV_GOOGLE"
            enumTypeId="DarpanChatProvider"
            enumCode="GOOGLE_CHAT"
            description="Google Chat"
            sequenceNum="1"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="CHAT_PROV_SLACK"
            enumTypeId="DarpanChatProvider"
            enumCode="SLACK"
            description="Slack"
            sequenceNum="2"/>

    <!-- DAR-BE-005 catalog of config types that can be shared across tenants.
         ConfigTenantAccess.configTypeEnumId FKs these; without them every grant dies on
         config_tenant_access_ibfk_2. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_HOTWAX_OMS"
            description="HotWax OMS REST source config (darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_SHOPIFY_AUTH"
            description="Shopify auth config (darpan.shopify.ShopifyAuthConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_NS_AUTH"
            description="NetSuite auth config (darpan.reconciliation.NsAuthConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration enumId="SCFG_NS_RESTLET"
            description="NetSuite Restlet config (darpan.reconciliation.NsRestletConfig)"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSharedConfigType"/>

    <!-- Source-system enums. OMS and SHOPIFY are RESTATEMENTS (description correction, see header)
         and must also precede the rows below that name them in parentEnumId — a self-reference on
         Enumeration, so document order decides whether the load succeeds. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="OMS"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="HOTWAX"
            description="HotWax"
            sequenceNum="1"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="SHOPIFY"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="SHOPIFY"
            description="Shopify"
            sequenceNum="2"/>

    <!-- Endpoint enums grouped under those two parents. OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS is a restatement that
         adds parentEnumId; the other three are new. Each precedes the SourceSystemConnector row that
         references it by systemEnumId. -->
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="OMS_TRANSFER_ORDERS"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="HOTWAX_TRANSFER_ORDERS"
            description="HotWax Transfer Orders"
            sequenceNum="6"
            parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="HOTWAX_RECON_ORDERS"
            description="HotWax Orders (Reconciliation API)"
            sequenceNum="7"
            parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="OMS_RETURNS"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="HOTWAX_RETURNS"
            description="HotWax Returns (Reconciliation API)"
            sequenceNum="8"
            parentEnumId="OMS"/>
    <moqui.basic.Enumeration
            enumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            enumTypeId="DarpanSystemSource"
            enumCode="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            description="Shopify Order Return References"
            sequenceNum="9"
            parentEnumId="SHOPIFY"/>

    <!-- Anonymous forced-password-change entry point. Parent ArtifactGroup DARPAN_AUTH_API already
         exists in every deployed environment, so this row has no forward FK reference. -->
    <moqui.security.ArtifactGroupMember artifactGroupId="DARPAN_AUTH_API"
            artifactName="facade.AuthFacadeServices.change#ExpiredPassword" artifactTypeEnumId="AT_SERVICE" inheritAuthz="Y"/>

    <!-- Connector registry rows. Each depends on its enum above; each is depended on by the field
         rows below. -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector
            systemEnumId="DATABASE"
            extractServiceName="reconciliation.DatabaseExtractionServices.extract#DatabaseRecords"
            dateFromParameterName="windowStart"
            dateToParameterName="windowEnd"
            expectedSourceConfigType="DATABASE_QUERY"
            configParameterName="databaseSourceQueryId"
            configEntityName="darpan.database.DatabaseSourceQuery"
            healthCheckServiceName="facade.DatabaseFacadeServices.probe#DatabaseConnection"
            systemAliases="DATABASE,DB,DAR_SYS_DATABASE"
            preserveWindowInstants="N"
            enabled="Y"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector
            systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS"
            extractServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReconciliationOrders"
            dateFromParameterName="windowStart"
            dateToParameterName="windowEnd"
            expectedSourceConfigType="HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RECON"
            configParameterName="omsRestSourceConfigId"
            configEntityName="darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig"
            remoteId="HOTWAX_ORDERS_API"
            endpointLabel="Reconciliation Orders API"
            sendUrlTemplate="{baseUrl}/rest/s1/oms/reconciliationOrders"
            remoteSendServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReconciliationOrders"
            systemAliases="OMS_RECON_ORDERS,HOTWAX_RECON_ORDERS,DAR_SYS_OMS_RECON"
            preserveWindowInstants="N"
            keepFieldsParameterName="keepRecordFields"
            keepFieldsBase="orderId,orderName,externalId,grandTotal,orderDate,statusId"
            filterParameterName="sourceFilters"
            healthCheckServiceName="facade.HotWaxOmsFacadeServices.probe#HotWaxOmsConnection"
            enabled="Y"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector
            systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS"
            extractServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReturns"
            dateFromParameterName="windowStart"
            dateToParameterName="windowEnd"
            expectedSourceConfigType="HOTWAX_OMS_REST_RETURNS"
            configParameterName="omsRestSourceConfigId"
            configEntityName="darpan.hotwax.HotWaxOmsRestSourceConfig"
            remoteId="HOTWAX_ORDERS_API"
            endpointLabel="Reconciliation Returns API"
            sendUrlTemplate="{baseUrl}/rest/s1/oms/reconciliationReturns"
            remoteSendServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.extract#HotWaxOmsReturns"
            systemAliases="OMS_RETURNS,HOTWAX_RETURNS,DAR_SYS_OMS_RETURNS"
            preserveWindowInstants="N"
            keepFieldsParameterName="keepRecordFields"
            keepFieldsBase="returnId,shopifyReturnId,externalId,orderExternalId,statusId,entryDate,returnTotal,currencyUomId,returnChannelEnumId"
            filterParameterName="sourceFilters"
            healthCheckServiceName="facade.HotWaxOmsFacadeServices.probe#HotWaxOmsConnection"
            orderStateLookupServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.lookup#HotWaxOmsOrdersByExternalId"
            lookupServiceName="reconciliation.HotWaxOmsExtractionServices.lookup#HotWaxOmsReturnsByExternalId"
            lookupIdsParameterName="externalIds"
            lookupMaxIds="10000"
            enabled="Y"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector
            systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            extractServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.extract#ShopifyOrderReturnRefs"
            dateFromParameterName="windowStart"
            dateToParameterName="windowEnd"
            expectedSourceConfigType="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS_API"
            configParameterName="shopifyAuthConfigId"
            configEntityName="darpan.shopify.ShopifyAuthConfig"
            remoteId="SHOPIFY_REMOTE"
            endpointLabel="Shopify Return References"
            systemAliases="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS,SHOPIFY_RETURNS,DAR_SYS_SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS"
            preserveWindowInstants="N"
            keepFieldsBase="refundOrReturnId,refundOrReturnType,orderId,createdAt,orderCancelledAt,refundLineEverFulfilled"
            lookupServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.lookup#ShopifyRefundOrReturnIds"
            lookupIdsParameterName="refundOrReturnIds"
            lookupMaxIds="10000"
            enabled="Y"/>

    <!-- Rules-board field pills, moved out of Groovy constants into data. Every row FKs a
         SourceSystemConnector by systemEnumId: OMS and SHOPIFY already exist in deployed environments, the
         other three are created immediately above. -->
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderId"
            label="Order ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="1"
            description="OMS order identity. In keepFieldsBase."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderName"
            label="Order name" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="2"
            description="Operator-facing order name. In keepFieldsBase."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].externalId"
            label="External ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="3"
            description="Shopify reference stored on the OMS order. In keepFieldsBase."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].grandTotal"
            label="Grand total" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="4"
            description="In keepFieldsBase. Comparison only — not key-like."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderDate"
            label="Order date" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="5"
            description="In keepFieldsBase."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].statusId"
            label="Status" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="6"
            description="In keepFieldsBase."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].salesChannelEnumId"
            label="Sales channel" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="7"
            description="NOT in keepFieldsBase. Offered because exclusion filters run before projection on the
                legacy endpoint, so the raw field is testable. This is a shipping exclusion use case."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS" fieldPath="$.records[*].productStoreId"
            label="Product store" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="8"
            description="NOT in keepFieldsBase. Same reason as salesChannelEnumId."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderId"
            label="Order ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="1"
            description="Server-side projected by /rest/s1/oms/reconciliationOrders."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderName"
            label="Order name" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="2"
            description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].externalId"
            label="External ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="3"
            description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].grandTotal"
            label="Grand total" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="4" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderDate"
            label="Order date" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="5" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RECON_ORDERS" fieldPath="$.records[*].statusId"
            label="Status" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="6" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].returnId"
            label="Return ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="1"
            description="OMS return identity."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].shopifyReturnId"
            label="Shopify reference" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="2"
            description="PREFERRED join key. Holds whichever Shopify id is the reference — refund or return —
                despite the name, and unlike externalId it is populated on RETURN_REQUESTED returns that have
                no refund yet. Matches Shopify SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS's refundOrReturnId."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].externalId"
            label="Shopify refund or return ID (legacy)" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="3"
            description="The original join key — a Shopify refund id or, for a small number of returns, a return
                id instead. BLANK on returns with no refund yet, which is why shopifyReturnId above supersedes it.
                Kept as a candidate so existing rule sets keyed on it keep resolving."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderExternalId"
            label="Order external ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="4"
            description="Order spine — joins a return back to its order."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].statusId"
            label="Status" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="5" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].entryDate"
            label="Entry date" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="6" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].returnTotal"
            label="Return total" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="7" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].currencyUomId"
            label="Currency" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="8" description="Server-side projected."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="OMS_RETURNS" fieldPath="$.records[*].returnChannelEnumId"
            label="Return channel" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="9"
            description="Included in the endpoint's server-side projection, so a rule drawn on it sees a value.
                Remove if OMS narrows the projection or ships the RQ-24 server-side channel filter."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY" fieldPath="$.records[*].id"
            label="Order ID" fieldType="ID" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="1"
            description="Shopify order GID."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY" fieldPath="$.records[*].name"
            label="Order name" fieldType="String" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="2"
            description="Shopify order name."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" fieldPath="$.records[*].refundOrReturnId"
            label="Refund ID / Return ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="1"
            description="RENAMED 2026-08-18 (was '$.records[*].eventId', labelled 'Event ID' then 'Refund or
                Return ID'): 'event' is this extractor's internal abstraction, not a Shopify term, and it
                surfaced verbatim on the rules board, the run summary and the diff columns. bareId-normalized
                identity — a REFUND id when refundOrReturnType is REFUND, a RETURN id when it is RETURN.
                Matches OMS externalId whichever kind it is: the single join key for returns reconciliation,
                with no precedence rule needed on either side."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" fieldPath="$.records[*].refundOrReturnType"
            label="Refund or return" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="2"
            description="RENAMED 2026-08-18 (was '$.records[*].eventType'). REFUND or RETURN — identifies
                which kind of id refundOrReturnId carries on this row. Not a join key; useful for filtering
                or as a comparison field."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" fieldPath="$.records[*].orderId"
            label="Order ID" fieldType="string" isPrimaryIdCandidate="Y" sequenceNum="3"
            description="bareId(legacyResourceId ?: id) — the bare GID tail, matching the numeric Shopify
                reference the OMS side stores. Unchanged by the per-refund/per-return reshape; still a
                grouping / secondary key, not the join key."/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnectorField systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" fieldPath="$.records[*].createdAt"
            label="Refund or return created" fieldType="string" sequenceNum="4"
            description="RELABELLED (was 'Order created', then 'Event created'): the individual refund's or
                return's own creation date — a refund row carries the refund's createdAt, a return row
                carries the return's — never the order's creation date. Windowing filters on this field, not
                on any order-level date."/>

    <!-- One-time data migration registry. No DarpanMigrationPrereq rows exist yet; when they do,
         they must follow every DarpanMigration row. -->
    <darpan.migration.DarpanMigration migrationId="TENANT_NOTIF_SETTINGS" componentName="darpan"
